Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.05,0:00:13.45,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}On November 27th, 2023, a K-pop debut broke the internet.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.45,0:00:21.45,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Twenty-two point five nine million views in twenty-four hours — the most-watched debut music video in the history of the genre.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.45,0:00:23.06,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Six girls on stage.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.06,0:00:26.83,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Neon, chrome, choreography tuned to the frame.
Dialogue: 1,0:00:08.44,0:00:17.88,Receipt,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}22,590,104 views — first 24 hours
Dialogue: 1,0:00:17.88,0:00:27.32,Receipt,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}NOVEMBER 27, 2023
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.12,0:00:30.89,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}But if you knew what to look for, something was off.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.89,0:00:33.55,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Six voices on a seven-part arrangement.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.55,0:00:35.96,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}A formation choreographed for seven.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.96,0:00:42.21,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}And in the comments, the same question, over and over, in every language the internet speaks.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:43.50,0:00:50.68,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Eight days earlier, on November 15th, Y-G Entertainment had made an announcement that split its fandom in two.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:50.68,0:00:59.86,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Its most hyped trainee in a decade — a fifteen-year-old the internet had already nicknamed the next great idol — would not be debuting with her group.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.86,0:01:00.97,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Health reasons.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.97,0:01:02.29,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}No return date.
Dialogue: 1,0:00:43.90,0:00:53.53,Receipt,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}NOVEMBER 15, 2023
Dialogue: 1,0:00:53.53,0:01:03.16,Receipt,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}YG ENTERTAINMENT OFFICIAL STATEMENT
Dialogue: 0,0:01:03.96,0:01:06.13,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Her name was Jung AH-hyun.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.13,0:01:10.77,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}She was fourteen months away from headlining an arena, three years from a dome.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.77,0:01:16.76,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}This is the story of the most-watched debut in K-pop history — the one that happened without her.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.76,0:01:20.02,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}And of the wait that turned a trainee into a headliner.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:22.47,0:01:23.32,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}CHUN-chon.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:23.32,0:01:27.41,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Capital of Gangwon Province, two hours north of Seoul by train.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:27.41,0:01:28.41,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}A lake city.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:28.41,0:01:29.23,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Quiet.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:29.23,0:01:32.33,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Famous for noodles and duck boats, not idols.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:32.33,0:01:40.46,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}In the last twenty years, virtually every K-pop star has been mined from Seoul, Busan, or overseas casting calls.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:40.46,0:01:42.31,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Almost nobody comes from here.
Dialogue: 1,0:01:22.87,0:01:32.74,Receipt,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}CHUNCHEON, GANGWON-DO
Dialogue: 1,0:01:32.74,0:01:42.61,Receipt,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}POP. ~280,000
Dialogue: 0,0:01:43.41,0:01:48.03,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Jung AH-hyun was born there on April 11th, 2007.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:48.03,0:02:01.74,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}By the account later put out around her debut, she was a child who performed before she could properly read — musical theater first, then singing, then rap, absorbing English from age five and Mandarin from seven.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:01.74,0:02:05.98,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}A trilingual kid from a lake city with a voice that did not sound local.
Dialogue: 1,0:01:43.81,0:02:06.26,Receipt,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}BORN APRIL 11, 2007
Dialogue: 0,0:02:07.06,0:02:11.83,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}To understand what happened next, you have to understand what Y-G Entertainment is.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:11.83,0:02:17.76,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}In the 2010s and 2020s it built BLACKPINK — the biggest girl group on the planet.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:17.76,0:02:20.49,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Y-G's entire brand is scarcity.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:20.49,0:02:21.69,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Few debuts.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:21.69,0:02:22.76,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Long training.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:22.76,0:02:24.31,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Editorial patience.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:24.31,0:02:29.82,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}When Y-G announces a girl group, the industry treats it like a product launch from Apple.
Dialogue: 1,0:02:07.46,0:02:18.88,Receipt,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}YG ENTERTAINMENT
Dialogue: 1,0:02:18.88,0:02:30.30,Receipt,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}HOME OF BIGBANG · 2NE1 · BLACKPINK
Dialogue: 0,0:02:31.10,0:02:36.95,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}By 2018, the machinery behind that brand had started turning on its next project.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:36.95,0:02:39.12,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Internally: the next girl group.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:39.12,0:02:40.69,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Externally: nothing.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:40.69,0:02:42.26,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}For years, nothing.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:42.26,0:02:43.89,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Y-G does not leak.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:43.89,0:02:45.15,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Y-G waits.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:45.15,0:02:51.71,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}And somewhere in that silence, a pre-teen from CHUN-chon walked into an audition room and changed her own life.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:53.00,0:02:56.12,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}She signed as a trainee at around eleven years old.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:56.12,0:03:03.59,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}What followed were five years of the Y-G system — the same assembly line that forged 2NE1 and BLACKPINK.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.59,0:03:07.67,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Vocal reps. Rap reps. Dance until the mirrors fog.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:07.67,0:03:12.90,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Monthly evaluations where one bad performance can freeze your file for a year.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:12.90,0:03:14.62,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Most trainees wash out.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:14.62,0:03:16.61,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}The system is designed that way.
Dialogue: 1,0:02:53.40,0:03:17.11,Receipt,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}5 YEARS OF TRAINING
Dialogue: 0,0:03:17.91,0:03:22.22,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}And through all five of those years, the public never knew she existed.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:22.22,0:03:23.63,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}No survival show.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:23.63,0:03:24.83,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}No rumor mill.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:24.83,0:03:28.65,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Just a locked file inside a company famous for locked files.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:28.65,0:03:37.88,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}It is one of the strangest quirks of this story: K-pop's most anticipated debut of the decade belonged to a girl whose name had never once trended.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:39.57,0:03:42.91,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}The audition circuit that produced her is its own economy.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:42.91,0:03:49.50,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Hundreds of thousands of Korean kids audition every year across the big agencies and the mid-tier ones.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:49.50,0:03:54.63,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Of those signed, the large majority are released from their contracts before debut.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:54.63,0:04:03.12,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}The math is closer to elite athletics than to music school — early specialization, private coaching, and a pyramid with almost no middle.
Dialogue: 1,0:03:39.97,0:04:03.60,Receipt,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}THE PYRAMID
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.40,0:04:07.90,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}And Y-G's version of the pyramid is steeper than most.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:07.90,0:04:15.22,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}The company debuted exactly two girl groups in the fourteen years between 2NE1 and BABYMONSTER.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:15.22,0:04:18.45,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}That is the entire point — and the entire risk.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:18.45,0:04:21.44,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}When you launch that rarely, you cannot launch small.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:21.44,0:04:24.83,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Every debut is a bet of the label's whole reputation.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:24.83,0:04:31.12,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Which is why, in 2023, everything about this project was engineered to be oversized.
Dialogue: 1,0:04:04.80,0:04:31.99,Receipt,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}2NE1 (2009) → BLACKPINK (2016) → BABYMONSTER (2023)
Dialogue: 0,0:04:32.79,0:04:35.09,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}New Year's Day, 2023.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:35.09,0:04:41.25,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Y-G posts a trailer with a name and almost nothing else: BABYMONSTER — Next Movement.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:41.25,0:04:45.39,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Sixty seconds of silhouettes, studio footage, and a logo.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:45.39,0:04:46.61,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}No faces.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:46.61,0:04:47.68,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}No names.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:47.68,0:04:48.99,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}No debut date.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:48.99,0:04:56.63,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}It collected millions of views in days, because after seven years of waiting, the heirs to BLACKPINK finally had a name.
Dialogue: 1,0:04:33.19,0:04:45.16,Receipt,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}JANUARY 1, 2023
Dialogue: 1,0:04:45.16,0:04:57.13,Receipt,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}"BABYMONSTER — NEXT MOVEMENT"
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.93,0:04:59.54,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Then came the reveals.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:59.54,0:05:06.17,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}One member at a time, one performance film each, posted straight to YouTube like case files being opened.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:06.17,0:05:19.96,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}On January 12th, the second file unsealed: a fifteen-year-old from CHUN-chon, rapping and singing take after take in a practice room, with a control of dynamics that made comment sections stop pretending to be neutral.
Dialogue: 1,0:04:58.33,0:05:09.38,Receipt,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}JANUARY 12, 2023
Dialogue: 1,0:05:09.38,0:05:20.43,Receipt,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}SECOND MEMBER REVEALED — AGE 15
Dialogue: 0,0:05:21.23,0:05:23.60,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}The internet did what the internet does.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:23.60,0:05:25.22,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}It found her old clips.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:25.22,0:05:26.65,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}It froze frames.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:26.65,0:05:35.48,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}It compared her tone to the label's legends and crowned her within a week — little Jennie, they called her, after BLACKPINK's sharpest all-rounder.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:35.48,0:05:44.24,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}For a fifteen-year-old, that nickname was both a throne and a cage, though nobody framing it as a compliment understood the second part yet.
Dialogue: 1,0:05:21.63,0:05:44.73,Receipt,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}"LITTLE JENNIE"
Dialogue: 0,0:05:45.53,0:05:48.60,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Through spring, the full roster came into focus.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:48.60,0:05:52.09,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Seven members from Korea, Thailand, and Japan.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:52.09,0:05:52.97,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}ROO-kah.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:52.97,0:05:54.12,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}fah-REE-tah.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:54.12,0:05:55.04,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}AH-sah.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:55.04,0:05:56.02,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}AH-hyun.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:56.02,0:05:56.96,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}RAH-mee.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:56.96,0:05:57.94,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}ROH-rah.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.94,0:05:59.07,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}chee-KEE-tah.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:59.07,0:06:08.26,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Y-G's first girl group in seven years, built deliberately as seven — a number the company would later weld directly into the brand itself.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:08.26,0:06:13.35,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}On paper, the strongest rookie lineup any major label had fielded in a decade.
Dialogue: 1,0:05:45.93,0:05:59.89,Receipt,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}7 MEMBERS
Dialogue: 1,0:05:59.89,0:06:13.85,Receipt,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}KOREA · THAILAND · JAPAN
Dialogue: 0,0:06:14.66,0:06:16.07,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Spring became summer.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:16.07,0:06:27.47,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}In May 2023, a pre-debut song called Dream hit number one on Billboard's Hot Trending Songs chart — a song nobody could buy, performed by girls nobody could see yet.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:27.47,0:06:35.30,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}The YouTube channel crossed a million subscribers in fifty-two days, the fastest any K-pop girl group had ever done it.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:35.30,0:06:37.76,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}And the debut date kept not arriving.
Dialogue: 1,0:06:15.06,0:06:26.65,Receipt,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}MAY 2023 — "DREAM" #1 BILLBOARD HOT TRENDING
Dialogue: 1,0:06:26.65,0:06:38.25,Receipt,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}1M SUBS IN 52 DAYS — FASTEST GG EVER
Dialogue: 0,0:06:39.05,0:06:42.46,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}The reveal films themselves became objects of study.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:42.46,0:06:53.01,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Each member performed alone in a plain studio — one take, one lighting rig, no styling theatrics — because Y-G was selling raw material, not packaging.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:53.01,0:06:56.81,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}The comment sections turned into scouting combine reports.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:56.81,0:07:08.04,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Tone, breath control, stage instinct, star presence, scored frame by frame by an audience that had been trained by a decade of survival shows to know exactly what it was looking at.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:09.31,0:07:12.34,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}AH-hyun's file was the one that kept circulating.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:12.34,0:07:18.72,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}The rap segments landed with the cadence of someone who'd studied the label's founders, not just its stars.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:18.72,0:07:25.92,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}The vocal takes swung from chest voice into a light head register without the seams most trainees leave showing.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:25.92,0:07:33.34,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}And underneath the technique, the thing scouts call presence — the camera finding her even when she wasn't the one performing.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:35.03,0:07:38.54,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Behind closed doors, the final evaluations were running.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:38.54,0:07:47.14,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Y-G filmed them — seven trainees, performing for the founder's approval, the tapes later released as a series called Last Evaluation.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:47.14,0:07:51.68,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}What those tapes captured, nobody in the audience fully processed at the time.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:51.68,0:08:00.68,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Watch them back today and you are watching six girls audition for a debut that had already happened, and one girl auditioning for a group she would have to join late.
Dialogue: 1,0:07:35.43,0:08:01.73,Receipt,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}"LAST EVALUATION" (2023)
Dialogue: 0,0:08:02.53,0:08:10.79,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Then, mid-2023, a pre-debut cover landed on the channel and refused to leave the charts of the internet's attention.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:10.79,0:08:15.77,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}AH-hyun, alone with a microphone, singing Charlie Puth's Dangerously.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:15.77,0:08:17.11,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}No choreography.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:17.11,0:08:18.36,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}No safety net.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:18.36,0:08:23.58,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Just dynamics — a verse held in a whisper, a chorus that opened like a door.
Dialogue: 1,0:08:02.93,0:08:24.09,Receipt,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}"DANGEROUSLY" — CHARLIE PUTH COVER
Dialogue: 0,0:08:24.89,0:08:29.43,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Covers like this surface every week in K-pop and vanish by Friday.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:29.43,0:08:30.95,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}This one did the opposite.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:30.95,0:08:36.71,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}It moved through TikTok and Twitter in translations, stitched and reacted to for weeks.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:36.71,0:08:39.57,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}And then it reached the one person whose song it was.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:40.86,0:08:44.09,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Charlie Puth didn't just notice it — he adopted it.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:44.09,0:08:58.00,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}In interviews he praised the voice outright, and before the year was out, the connection had turned tangible: Puth wrote and gifted a song for the group, called Like That — a track widely understood to be his answer to that cover.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:58.00,0:09:04.72,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}A global pop star personally forwarding material because a fifteen-year-old's take on his song stopped him scrolling.
Dialogue: 1,0:08:41.26,0:08:53.33,Receipt,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}CHARLIE PUTH → "LIKE THAT"
Dialogue: 1,0:08:53.33,0:09:05.40,Receipt,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}GIFTED TO BABYMONSTER
Dialogue: 0,0:09:06.20,0:09:09.16,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Vocally, the cover was a statement of range.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:09.16,0:09:21.90,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Puth writes melodies that sit in an awkward middle zone — too low for pure belt, too high for comfort — and the Dangerously chorus demands you cross that zone in public, audibly, on camera.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:21.90,0:09:31.49,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Her version treated the verse as a whisper and the bridge as a launchpad, which is exactly the dynamics-first approach that later became her stage signature.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:32.78,0:09:36.82,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}The rollout metrics around her told the same story from the business side.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:36.82,0:09:44.36,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Pre-registration for the debut had become, per Y-G's own releases, the largest in the channel's history for a rookie act.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:44.36,0:09:52.42,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Brand anticipation indexes ranked a group that had performed zero official songs inside the top tier of upcoming launches.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:52.42,0:10:04.72,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}This is the part of K-pop outsiders consistently underestimate: by the time a group debuts, the market has already spent months pricing it — and the market had priced this one as the biggest launch of the year.
Dialogue: 1,0:09:33.18,0:10:05.38,Receipt,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}THE MARKET HAD PRICED IT
Dialogue: 0,0:10:06.18,0:10:12.63,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}By autumn 2023, the shape of the debut was public: November 27th. Batter Up.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:12.63,0:10:16.40,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}The most pre-registered debut in YouTube's K-pop history.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:16.40,0:10:20.04,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Advertisers had bought in before a single chorus had been heard.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:20.04,0:10:28.85,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}The rollout was a machine at full RPM — and Jung AH-hyun was in the center of the formation of every teaser released up to that point.
Dialogue: 1,0:10:06.58,0:10:29.54,Receipt,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}NOV 27, 2023 — "BATTER UP"
Dialogue: 0,0:10:30.34,0:10:33.14,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Two weeks before the date, the machine stopped.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:33.14,0:10:39.47,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}A statement from Y-G, brief as a telegram: AH-hyun would not participate in the debut.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:39.47,0:10:41.40,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Health and recovery first.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:41.40,0:10:44.25,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}No timeline offered, because there wasn't one.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:44.25,0:10:47.69,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}The comments under a debut teaser turned into a vigil.
Dialogue: 1,0:10:30.74,0:10:39.75,Receipt,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}NOVEMBER 15, 2023
Dialogue: 1,0:10:39.75,0:10:48.76,Receipt,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}OFFICIAL YG STATEMENT
Dialogue: 0,0:10:49.56,0:10:54.95,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Here is what most people outside K-pop miss about a missing member: the show does not stop.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:54.95,0:11:01.78,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}A debut is a years-long production with budgets, broadcast slots, and a launch window that cannot move.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:01.78,0:11:12.98,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}On November 27th, 2023, BABYMONSTER debuted as six — and the industry watched to see whether a seven-piece group with a hole in it could still break records.
Dialogue: 1,0:10:49.97,0:11:13.45,Receipt,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}DEBUT: 6 OF 7
Dialogue: 0,0:11:14.25,0:11:16.06,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Batter Up answered in one day.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:16.06,0:11:23.20,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Twenty-two point five nine million views in twenty-four hours — a record for any K-pop group debut, ever.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:23.20,0:11:25.79,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}One hundred million in eighteen days.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:25.79,0:11:32.38,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}The channel kept setting speed limits: fastest girl group to a million subscribers, fastest to two.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:32.38,0:11:34.16,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}The machine worked perfectly.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:34.16,0:11:41.69,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}And the entire time, the fastest-growing comment section on every upload was a countdown to a name that wasn't there.
Dialogue: 1,0:11:14.65,0:11:28.52,Receipt,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}22.59M — FIRST 24H
Dialogue: 1,0:11:28.52,0:11:42.39,Receipt,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}100M — FIRST 18 DAYS
Dialogue: 0,0:11:43.19,0:11:45.73,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}The debut era rolled on without pause.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:45.73,0:11:52.97,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Award-show rotations, year-end stages, brand shoots — a full rookie campaign executed at six.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:52.97,0:12:01.75,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Behind the scenes, the group's formation photographs kept one position subtly offset, the way teams do when a roster is known to change.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:01.75,0:12:04.61,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Fans read the framing like weather patterns.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:04.61,0:12:11.85,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}The company, to its credit, never once performed the absence — no tribute edits, no sympathy messaging.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:11.85,0:12:16.35,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}The work carried on, and the empty chair stayed empty in silence.
Dialogue: 1,0:11:43.59,0:12:17.04,Receipt,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}THE SIX-MEMBER ERA
Dialogue: 0,0:12:17.84,0:12:22.67,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}For the members themselves, the period demanded a specific kind of discipline.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:22.67,0:12:33.92,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Six teenagers, some of them fifteen and sixteen, answering interview questions about a seventh member they shared a dorm practice schedule with — day after day, market after market.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:33.92,0:12:42.64,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Their collective answer became a running theme of the debut era: she is part of this, the formation is temporary, the group is seven.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:42.64,0:12:48.17,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Said differently by every member, in every language, for four straight months.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:49.65,0:12:59.09,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}In February 2024, the pre-debut single Stuck In The Middle showed a softer register — and AH-hyun's absence on it said more than any statement.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:59.09,0:13:04.02,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Fans began tracking her like astronomers tracking an object behind the sun.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:04.02,0:13:05.47,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Sightings: none.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:05.47,0:13:06.93,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Statements: none.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:06.93,0:13:10.61,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}But if you knew Y-G's patterns, the silence had a shape.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:10.61,0:13:14.64,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}The company had done this before, with artists it intended to keep.
Dialogue: 1,0:12:50.05,0:13:15.32,Receipt,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}FEB 1, 2024 — "STUCK IN THE MIDDLE"
Dialogue: 0,0:13:16.12,0:13:18.50,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}The fandom organized around the gap.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:18.50,0:13:22.38,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Message boards ran recovery wishes in a dozen languages.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:22.38,0:13:26.23,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Fan projects adopted her symbol before there was an official one.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:26.23,0:13:34.21,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}And in March 2024, the company that never leaks let one sentence out of the building: the seventh member was returning.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:34.21,0:13:36.25,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}The debut had been a launch window.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:36.25,0:13:37.51,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}This was the payload.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:39.00,0:13:41.94,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}The announcement itself was three sentences long.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:41.94,0:13:44.81,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}No video, no teaser, no photo.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:44.81,0:13:58.26,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}In an industry that bills a member's return as a comeback special with countdown content, Y-G handled the most anticipated return of the year like a press release from a different decade — and the restraint read as confidence.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:58.26,0:14:03.00,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}The fans who had spent four months organizing welcome projects didn't get a warning.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:03.00,0:14:04.01,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}They got a date.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:05.49,0:14:14.13,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}The vehicle for the return had a name engineered for exactly this moment: BABY-MON-SEVEN-ER — the seven welded into the word itself.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:14.13,0:14:15.50,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}First mini album.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:15.50,0:14:17.89,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}April 1st, 2024.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:17.89,0:14:20.37,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Not a comeback, in any real sense.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:20.37,0:14:24.66,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}A debut, done twice, with the missing frequency restored.
Dialogue: 1,0:14:05.89,0:14:15.72,Receipt,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}APRIL 1, 2024
Dialogue: 1,0:14:15.72,0:14:25.54,Receipt,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}BABYMONS7ER
Dialogue: 0,0:14:26.34,0:14:31.04,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}SHEESH opened with a bass line like a dropped gate and a hook built for stadiums.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:31.04,0:14:46.41,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}The music video passed two hundred million views in under a year and change — and on April 17th, 2026, it would become the fastest girl-group debut MV ever to four hundred million, doing it in seven hundred and forty-seven days.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:46.41,0:14:51.05,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}But the number that mattered most in April 2024 wasn't a view count.
Dialogue: 1,0:14:26.75,0:14:51.53,Receipt,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}"SHEESH" — APR 1, 2024
Dialogue: 0,0:14:52.33,0:15:01.59,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}It was this: after one hundred and thirty-eight days of silence, Jung AH-hyun was singing again — and this time, officially, in the center.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:01.59,0:15:04.11,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}The arrangements suddenly made sense.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:04.11,0:15:06.54,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}The seven-part harmonies had their seventh.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:06.54,0:15:09.84,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Choreographers stopped designing around empty air.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:09.84,0:15:15.70,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}For the first time since January 2023, BABYMONSTER was mathematically complete.
Dialogue: 1,0:15:17.39,0:15:41.36,Receipt,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}CIRCLE ALBUM CHART — #3
Dialogue: 0,0:15:42.15,0:15:45.31,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Live, the SHEESH era made the case in person.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:45.31,0:15:57.25,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Her stage rap in the second verse drew a hard line under the vocal-versus-rapper question — the flip from sung chorus into a tightened, percussive delivery became the clip that editors reached for first.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:57.25,0:16:01.77,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Vocally, the belt at the final hook became the moment crowds came to film.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:01.77,0:16:05.79,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}A star turn, executed in month one of the actual career.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:07.28,0:16:09.73,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Then came the strangest track on the album.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:09.73,0:16:15.52,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Like That — the song Charlie Puth wrote after the Dangerously cover went through him like a current.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:15.52,0:16:19.73,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Her cover had reached the writer; the writer had answered with new material.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:19.73,0:16:29.62,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Very few careers contain a loop that clean: a fifteen-year-old sings a song into the internet, and two years later the author of that song hands her the sequel.
Dialogue: 1,0:16:07.68,0:16:18.99,Receipt,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}COVER → GIFT → RECORD
Dialogue: 1,0:16:18.99,0:16:30.30,Receipt,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}DANGEROUSLY → "LIKE THAT"
Dialogue: 0,0:16:31.10,0:16:33.29,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}The press cycle had its own gravity.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:33.29,0:16:42.18,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}In debut interviews she was asked, inevitably, about the nickname — little Jennie, the comparison to the label's most famous all-rounder.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:42.18,0:16:47.70,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Her answer became the most quoted sentence of her first year: that she hoped to find her own color.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:47.70,0:16:49.22,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}It is a small sentence.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:49.22,0:16:52.12,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}It is also the entire plot of what came next.
Dialogue: 1,0:16:31.50,0:16:53.00,Receipt,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}"I HOPE TO FIND MY OWN COLOR"
Dialogue: 0,0:16:53.80,0:17:00.48,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Finding your own color, in idol terms, is not a metaphor — it is a production problem with a deadline.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:00.48,0:17:10.13,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}It means the arrangement of your voice inside the group's sound: which frequencies you claim, which registers you lend to harmonies, which ad-libs are yours by law.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:10.13,0:17:16.30,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Comparisons blur that map, because a comparison asks you to occupy someone else's frequencies.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:16.30,0:17:18.50,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}The fix is not to imitate less.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:18.50,0:17:25.15,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}It is to write parts that only one person can sing — and then sing them until the map redraws itself.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:26.82,0:17:30.01,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Because the industry was already scoring her against it.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:30.01,0:17:37.59,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Idol survival culture in Korea runs on comparison — vocal tone versus tone, screen time versus screen time.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:37.59,0:17:43.94,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}For every comment celebrating her range, there was a spreadsheet measuring her against BLACKPINK's timeline.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:43.94,0:17:47.77,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}The nickname had given her a head start and a debt at the same time.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:47.77,0:17:52.98,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Her response, over the next twenty-four months, was to make the spreadsheets irrelevant.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:54.48,0:17:59.61,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}July 2024 brought Forever — a summer single that let the vocals breathe.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:59.61,0:18:05.00,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}November 1st, 2024 brought the first full-length statement: DRIP.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:05.00,0:18:07.99,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Eight hundred twenty thousand first-week copies.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:07.99,0:18:10.06,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}A million in domestic sales.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:10.06,0:18:13.13,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Billboard 200 entry at one forty-nine.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:13.13,0:18:15.27,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}RIAJ platinum in Japan.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:15.27,0:18:24.91,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}And on the title track, a guest verse from G-Dragon — the king of the label personally appearing on the heirs' record, which in Y-G terms is a coronation.
Dialogue: 1,0:17:54.88,0:18:05.12,Receipt,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}NOV 1, 2024 — DRIP
Dialogue: 1,0:18:05.12,0:18:15.36,Receipt,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}820K FIRST WEEK · 1M+ DOMESTIC
Dialogue: 1,0:18:15.36,0:18:25.59,Receipt,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}BILLBOARD 200 #149
Dialogue: 0,0:18:26.39,0:18:32.39,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Before DRIP, though, came the summer single that taught the fanbase how to miss a song on purpose.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:32.39,0:18:39.62,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Forever was built light — retro synth, open vowels, a chorus that asked to be sung in a stadium parking lot.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:39.62,0:18:51.03,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}It was also, quietly, a demo of the group's post-hiatus chemistry: parts arranged to interlock seven ways, with the seventh voice threaded through harmonies instead of stacked above them.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:51.03,0:18:55.31,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Arrangers write differently when the full instrument finally exists.
Dialogue: 1,0:18:26.79,0:18:56.00,Receipt,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}JUL 1, 2024 — "FOREVER"
Dialogue: 0,0:18:56.79,0:19:01.07,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}But the number that redefined the group came in January 2025.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:01.07,0:19:11.15,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}On the 25th, the Hello Monsters world tour opened at Seoul's K-S-P-O Dome — the Olympic gymnastics arena that functions as K-pop's certification board.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:11.15,0:19:15.79,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Fastest female act ever to headline it: eight months after debut.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:15.79,0:19:20.47,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Three hundred thousand tickets across thirty-two shows in twenty cities followed.
Dialogue: 1,0:18:57.20,0:19:09.18,Receipt,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}JAN 25, 2025 — KSPO DOME
Dialogue: 1,0:19:09.18,0:19:21.16,Receipt,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}FASTEST FEMALE ACT EVER TO HEADLINE — 8 MONTHS
Dialogue: 0,0:19:21.96,0:19:30.37,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}2025 rolled forward: Hot Sauce in July, a tribute threaded to Seo Taiji, the founding father of Korean pop.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:30.37,0:19:31.82,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}We Go Up in October.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:31.82,0:19:36.57,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}The group was now releasing at BLACKPINK cadence with a touring operation to match.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:36.57,0:19:44.92,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}And AH-hyun's position in it had quietly changed — the girl once booked as the next someone was now being booked as the first AH-hyun.
Dialogue: 1,0:19:22.36,0:19:33.88,Receipt,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}JUL 2025 — "HOT SAUCE"
Dialogue: 1,0:19:33.88,0:19:45.39,Receipt,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}OCT 10, 2025 — WE GO UP
Dialogue: 0,0:19:46.19,0:19:48.58,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Tour life restructured the group's year.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:48.58,0:19:58.68,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Thirty-two shows across Asia means airport departures, arena load-ins, and rest days measured in hotel hours — a rhythm that ages rookies fast.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:58.68,0:20:08.19,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Setlists from the tour's first leg show the engineering: each member rotated through solo moments built to showcase a different register of the group's sound.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:08.19,0:20:17.48,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}AH-hyun's slot drew the loudest documented reactions of the run, and the fan-cam economy did the rest, one four-minute vertical video at a time.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:18.97,0:20:23.22,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Then, November 2025, the MAMA Awards in Hong Kong.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:23.22,0:20:33.73,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Three members — AH-hyun, fah-REE-tah, ROH-rah — performed a medley from KPop Demon Hunters, covering Golden at the biggest award show in Asia.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:33.73,0:20:39.55,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}The clip did six point six eight million views and became the night's most-watched performance.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:39.55,0:20:46.37,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}And then the internet did what it does: the praise lasted a day, and the discourse about live vocals lasted a week.
Dialogue: 1,0:20:19.37,0:20:33.20,Receipt,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}MAMA 2025 — "GOLDEN" MEDLEY
Dialogue: 1,0:20:33.20,0:20:47.03,Receipt,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}6.68M VIEWS — TOP PERFORMANCE OF THE NIGHT
Dialogue: 0,0:20:47.83,0:20:49.36,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Here is the part worth keeping.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:49.36,0:20:50.79,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}She did not hide from it.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:50.79,0:21:01.33,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Within weeks she was on music shows singing with a hand-held mic and no ear monitors — the most exposed setup an idol can choose — and letting the results post themselves.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:01.33,0:21:08.13,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Whatever else 2026 would bring, the answer to November's discourse had already been filed in December.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:09.81,0:21:12.70,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}2026 did not begin with a song.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:12.70,0:21:14.25,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}It began with a chart.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:14.25,0:21:27.52,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}In January, Really Like You — a track from the previous autumn — climbed to number one on YouTube's global viral fifty, driven entirely by fan edits and short-form covers, months after release.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:27.52,0:21:30.30,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Industry people call it a reverse chart run.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:30.30,0:21:33.72,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}It is what happens when an audience decides a song isn't done.
Dialogue: 1,0:21:10.21,0:21:22.22,Receipt,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}JAN 2026 — "REALLY LIKE YOU"
Dialogue: 1,0:21:22.22,0:21:34.23,Receipt,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}#1 YOUTUBE GLOBAL VIRAL 50
Dialogue: 0,0:21:35.03,0:21:39.31,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}March brought Vogue Hong Kong, and a cover titled The Only Way Is Up.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:39.31,0:21:40.94,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Not a K-pop magazine.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:40.94,0:21:42.48,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Not a fan service shoot.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:42.48,0:21:49.14,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Vogue — the fashion industry's front page — putting a nineteen-year-old from CHUN-chon on its March issue.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:49.14,0:21:56.61,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}In the same quarter: a Taipei encore where she addressed the arena in Mandarin, the language she'd studied since she was seven.
Dialogue: 1,0:21:35.43,0:21:46.27,Receipt,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}MARCH 2026 — VOGUE HONG KONG
Dialogue: 1,0:21:46.27,0:21:57.11,Receipt,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}"THE ONLY WAY IS UP"
Dialogue: 0,0:21:57.91,0:22:00.71,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}The Mandarin moment deserves its own footnote.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:00.71,0:22:11.38,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}At the Taipei encore, mid-tour, she addressed the arena in Mandarin — not a rehearsed greeting, by every account, but long enough to count as crowd work.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:11.38,0:22:25.22,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Trilingual stage presence is rare in any generation of idol; using the third language as a connective gesture toward the audience that showed up for you is the kind of detail that converts casual viewers into permanent ones.
Dialogue: 1,0:21:58.31,0:22:25.91,Receipt,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}TAIPEI ARENA — MANDARIN ENCORE
Dialogue: 0,0:22:26.71,0:22:29.74,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}April was the month the receipts stacked vertically.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:29.74,0:22:35.15,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}First, the Korea Grand Music Awards, where fans don't nominate — they vote.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:35.15,0:22:43.95,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Artist of April, solo female category: thirty-three thousand three hundred and eighty votes, eighty-five point eight one percent of the total.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:43.95,0:22:54.22,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Then, on the seventeenth, the trade press confirmed it: SHEESH had crossed four hundred million views, faster than any girl-group debut video ever recorded.
Dialogue: 1,0:22:27.11,0:22:41.00,Receipt,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}KGMA — 33,380 VOTES (85.81%)
Dialogue: 1,0:22:41.00,0:22:54.89,Receipt,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}APR 17, 2026 — "SHEESH" 400M
Dialogue: 0,0:22:55.69,0:23:03.58,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}The KGMA result deserves its own arithmetic, because fan-voted awards measure something charts can't: mobilization.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:03.58,0:23:16.45,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Thirty-three thousand votes in a solo category means fanbases coordinating across time zones, on apps, against other mobilized fanbases — and eighty-five percent of the share means it wasn't close.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:16.45,0:23:23.33,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}For a member whose fandom identity was built during four months of waiting, the vote was the wait, cashed in.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:24.82,0:23:29.40,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}May brought the third mini album: CHOOM — Korean for dance.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:29.40,0:23:38.53,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}July brought the statistic that would have been unthinkable at debut: number thirty-five on the US Mediabase Top 40, the American radio chart.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:38.53,0:23:41.74,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}First BABYMONSTER entry.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:41.74,0:23:48.44,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}K-pop's gatekeeping metric, measured not in YouTube views but in actual spins on US stations.
Dialogue: 1,0:23:25.22,0:23:37.08,Receipt,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}MAY 4, 2026 — CHOOM
Dialogue: 1,0:23:37.08,0:23:48.95,Receipt,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}JUL 2026 — MEDIABASE TOP 40 #35
Dialogue: 0,0:23:49.75,0:23:57.08,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Mediabase deserves a plain-language translation, because it is the least glamorous and most serious number in the story.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:57.08,0:24:03.30,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}It counts actual radio spins — airplay logged from monitored stations across the United States.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:03.30,0:24:07.75,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}No streaming bundles, no fan purchasing power, no algorithm.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:07.75,0:24:12.67,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Real programmers, playing a Korean-language title track in daytime rotation.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:12.67,0:24:22.09,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}For a genre that spent two decades being told its ceiling was the internet, charting on US radio in year three is the kind of line that ends arguments.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:23.77,0:24:32.34,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}June's single SUGAR HONEY ICE TEA went to number one on YouTube's global daily music chart and sprinted past a hundred million views.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:32.34,0:24:42.94,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}And on TikTok, a piece of choreography from the CHOOM era detached itself from the song entirely — the AH-hyun March, a stride so distinctive it became a format.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:42.94,0:24:44.69,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Millions of imitations.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:44.69,0:24:46.30,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Brazilian funk edits.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:46.30,0:24:49.42,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}A walk, literally, copied around the world.
Dialogue: 1,0:24:24.17,0:24:37.14,Receipt,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}"SUGAR HONEY ICE TEA" — #1 GLOBAL DAILY
Dialogue: 1,0:24:37.14,0:24:50.11,Receipt,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}THE AHYEON MARCH
Dialogue: 0,0:24:50.91,0:24:58.53,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}The March itself is worth forty seconds of analysis, because virality of this kind is engineering plus accident.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:58.53,0:25:08.18,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}The move is simple enough to learn in one watch — a stride, a shoulder line, a snap of the chin — and distinctive enough to read at thumbnail size.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:08.18,0:25:19.08,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Short-form platforms reward exactly that signature: recognizable in half a second, copyable in ten seconds, hard to do well, which keeps the imitations coming.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:19.08,0:25:25.47,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}The name attached to it traveled the way names do now — first a joke, then a tag, then a fact.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:26.95,0:25:35.51,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}And on September 3rd, 2026, the number behind all the numbers arrived: the channel passed ten billion cumulative views.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:35.51,0:25:38.88,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Second K-pop girl group in history to get there.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:38.88,0:25:39.88,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Fastest.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:39.88,0:25:45.46,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}A catalog barely three years old, outpacing channels that had a decade's head start.
Dialogue: 1,0:25:27.35,0:25:36.94,Receipt,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}SEP 3, 2026 — 10 BILLION VIEWS
Dialogue: 1,0:25:36.94,0:25:46.52,Receipt,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}FASTEST GG CHANNEL EVER — 2ND EVER TO 10B
Dialogue: 0,0:25:47.32,0:25:58.90,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Context for ten billion: the only K-pop girl group channel ahead of it belongs to BLACKPINK, and that channel needed eight years and one of the most dominant runs in music history to get there.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:58.90,0:26:05.31,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}BABYMONSTER crossed the line in roughly three, on the strength of a catalog of barely thirty songs.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:05.31,0:26:13.01,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}The pace, not the total, is the story — and the pace is what makes the next decade of projections genuinely unstable.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:14.68,0:26:18.67,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}September 22nd and 23rd, 2026.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:18.67,0:26:21.04,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}KEE-oh-seh-rah Dome, Osaka.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:21.04,0:26:26.35,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Fifty-five thousand seats, a structure that has hosted the biggest acts on the planet.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:26.35,0:26:32.00,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}For a K-pop group, headlining a Japanese dome is not a tour stop — it is a rank.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:32.00,0:26:35.58,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}BABYMONSTER arrived there in year three of their career.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:35.58,0:26:41.06,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}For the girl from CHUN-chon who missed the debut, it was the first headline of the next decade.
Dialogue: 1,0:26:15.08,0:26:28.41,Receipt,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}SEP 22–23, 2026
Dialogue: 1,0:26:28.41,0:26:41.74,Receipt,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}KYOCERA DOME, OSAKA
Dialogue: 0,0:26:42.53,0:26:45.89,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Zoom out, and the shape of the story is almost absurd.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:45.89,0:26:48.49,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}A debut that broke records without her.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:48.49,0:26:50.05,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Four months of silence.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:50.05,0:26:52.12,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}A return that doubled the debut.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:52.12,0:26:55.31,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}A nickname she retired by becoming uncomparable.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:55.31,0:27:02.28,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Records for views, votes, radio, and domes — most of them still marked fastest in history.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:02.28,0:27:04.60,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}All of it before her twentieth birthday.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:06.09,0:27:11.35,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}It is worth saying plainly what the last three years actually contained, because speed blinds.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:11.35,0:27:19.47,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}A fifteen-year-old announced as a label's future, then removed from the biggest launch of her company's decade for reasons she never controlled.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:19.47,0:27:23.87,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Four months of public silence at an age when most careers haven't started.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:23.87,0:27:29.03,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}A return under the heaviest comparison nickname the internet could manufacture.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:29.03,0:27:40.22,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}And then — instead of the cautious, managed mediocrity that usually follows a health pause — a run of records, covers, charts, and domes executed at full sprint.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:41.90,0:27:45.65,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}The most-watched debut in K-pop history was missing someone.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:45.65,0:27:50.17,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Three years later, the missing one is the reason nobody can stop watching.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:50.17,0:27:51.50,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}She is nineteen.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:51.50,0:27:52.76,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}The dome is open.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:52.76,0:28:01.71,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}And the story, as her fans like to say — the ones who waited, the ones who never stopped asking where she was — is very much still being written.
Dialogue: 1,0:27:42.30,0:27:52.14,Receipt,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}SHE IS 19
Dialogue: 1,0:27:52.14,0:28:01.99,Receipt,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}THE STORY IS STILL BEING WRITTEN
Dialogue: 0,0:28:02.79,0:28:10.50,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}The butterfly has become the thing her fans carry — the official symbol of a fandom that learned patience as a group activity.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:10.50,0:28:13.67,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}It fits, in a way that branding rarely does.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:13.67,0:28:22.42,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}A thing that spends its early life unrecognizable from what it becomes, and arrives on the other side of the wait with entirely new wings.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:22.42,0:28:24.54,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}You can call that a metaphor if you like.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:24.54,0:28:27.36,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Her fans call it a record of what actually happened.
Dialogue: 1,0:28:03.19,0:28:28.43,Receipt,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}FOR THE MONSTIEZ 🦋
Dialogue: 0,0:28:29.24,0:28:34.64,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}If this film earned it, subscribe — the next documentary is already in production.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:34.64,0:28:37.74,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(140,140)}Sources for every figure are in the description.